Azure Monitor alerts help administrators detect important conditions in Azure resources and applications. Alerts can evaluate metrics or other monitoring signals and trigger actions when defined conditions are met.

An alert configuration generally involves:

* Signal
* Condition
* Threshold
* Evaluation period
* Severity
* Action group

Action groups define what happens when an alert is triggered, such as sending notifications or initiating an automated response.

For example, an administrator can configure an alert when a production virtual machine's CPU remains above 90% for a sustained period.

A real-life use case is an operations team receiving immediate notifications about performance problems before users report application failures.

Alerts transform monitoring data into actionable operational responses.
